hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22696","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Dam'aj, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people are led by the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah; then if they are equal in recitation, the most knowing of them of the Sunnah, then the earliest of them in migration; then if they are equal in migration, the eldest of them in age. And do not lead a man in his authority, nor sit upon his honored seat in his house until he permits you."
"22697","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, who said: al-Dastuwai informed us, and Yazid informed us: al-Dastuwai informed us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to pray witr from the first of the night, its middle, and its end."
"22698","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, my father narrated to me, from Hakim ibn Aflah, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: For the Muslim upon the Muslim are four traits: That he answer him when he calls him, invoke mercy for him when he sneezes, visit him when he is ill, and witness him when he dies."
"22699","Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, Qays narrated to us, from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointed with his hand toward Yemen and said: Faith is here, faith is here; and harshness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen at the roots of the tails of camels, where the two horns of Satan rise, in Rabi'ah and Mudar."
"22700","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Mas'ud Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I stay behind from the morning prayer because of so-and-so, from what he lengthens for us. Then I never saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more severe in anger in admonition than him that day. Then he said: O people, among you are repellers; so whichever of you prays with the people, let him lighten, for among them are the weak, the old, and the one with need."
"22701","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan, Mansur narrated to us from Ribi from Abu Masud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: From what people have retained of the words of the first prophethood: if you feel no shame, do whatever you wish."
"22702","Additions of al-Qatii: Ibn Malik said: al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us from Ribi from Abu Masud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed from what people have retained of the words of the first prophethood: if you feel no shame, do whatever you wish."
"22703","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us from al-Amash from Shaqiq from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order charity, so one of us would go out to carry loads for hire and bring back a mudd, and today some of them have a hundred thousand. Shaqiq said: So I saw that he was hinting at himself."
"22704","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from Abdullah ibn Yazid from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man spending on his family, seeking reward for it, is charity."
"22705","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Salamah from Iyad ibn Iyad from his father from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us with a sermon, so he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Among you are hypocrites, so whomever I name, let him stand. Then he said: Stand, O so-and-so, stand, O so-and-so, stand, O so-and-so, until he named thirty-six men. Then he said: Among you, or from you, so fear Allah. He said: So Umar passed by a veiled man among those he named whom he had known, he said: What is wrong with you? He said: So he told him what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, so he said: Away with you for the rest of the day."
"22706","Abu Nuaim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Salamah from a man from his father, Sufyan said: I think he is Iyad ibn Iyad, from his father from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, and he mentioned its meaning."
"22707","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman from Ibrahim al-Taymi from his father from Abu Masud that he was beating a boy of his, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: By Allah, Allah is more capable over you than you are over him. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I free him for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"22708","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Abu Masud that he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he said: I have nothing to give you, but go to so-and-so. So the man went to him and he gave him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good has like the reward of its doer, or its worker."
"22709","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed me from Nuaim ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, in the hadith of Abd al-Rahman, and Abdullah ibn Zayd is the one who was shown the call to prayer, informed him from Abu Masud al-Ansari that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in the gathering of Sad ibn Ubadah, so Bashir ibn Sad said to him: Allah has commanded us to pray upon you, O Messenger of Allah, so how do we pray upon you? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent until we wished he had not asked him. Then he said: Say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim in the worlds, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And the salam is as you have known."
"22710","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik ibn Anas from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz delayed the prayer one day, so Urwah ibn al-Zubayr entered upon him and told him that al-Mughirah ibn Shubah delayed the prayer one day while in Kufa, so Abu Masud al-Ansari entered upon him and said: What is this, O Mughirah, do you not know that Jibril, peace be upon him, descended and prayed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then he prayed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then he said: With this I was commanded. So Umar said to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: Know what you narrate, O Urwah, was Jibril the one who established the time of prayer for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Urwah said: That is how Bashir ibn Abi Masud used to narrate from his father."
"22711","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Amash from Ibrahim al-Taymi from his father from Abu Masud who said: While I was beating a slave of mine, suddenly a man calling behind me: Know, O Abu Masud, know, O Abu Masud. So I turned, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: By Allah, Allah is more capable over you than you are over this one. He said: So I swore I would never beat a slave of mine again."
"22712","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from al-Qasim ibn al-Harith from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: This authority will remain among you, and you are its rulers, until you commit deeds, and when you do that, Allah will set over you the worst of His creation, so they will peel you as the stick is peeled."
"22713","Abu Nuaim narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Utbah who said: So they will peel you, and likewise Abu Ahmad said, and he said: So they will peel you. Abu Nuaim said: As the stick is peeled."
"22714","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Abu Masud that a man gave charity with a haltered she-camel in the cause of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will surely come, or she will surely come, with seven hundred haltered she-camels."
"22715","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman who said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani, and he mentioned it without doubt, he said: She will surely come."
"22716","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us from Ata ibn al-Saib, Salim al-Barrad narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Abu Masud al-Ansari and asked him about prayer, so he said: Shall I not pray with you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray? He said: So he stood, said takbir, and raised his hands, then bowed and placed his palms on his knees and kept his armpits apart. He said: Then he stood until everything of him was settled, then prostrated and placed his palms and kept his armpits apart. He said: Then he stood until everything of him was settled, then he prayed four rakahs like this."
"22717","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Abu Masud, he raised it, and Shadhan once said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One consulted is entrusted."
"22718","And Shadhan also mentioned the hadith of one who guides to good is as its doer."
"22719","Abu Nuaim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from al-Qasim ibn al-Harith from Abdullah ibn Utbah from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: This authority will remain among you, and you are its rulers, as long as you do not commit innovations. And when you do that, Allah will set over you the worst of His creation, and they will peel you as the stick is peeled."
